ALTER TABLE categories ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS content_html TEXT;

UPDATE categories
SET content_html = '<h2>3 Seater Sofa Collection</h2>
<p>Most Pakistani living rooms get built around one piece first, and it is usually the 3 seater sofa. Everything else, the side tables, the rug, the chairs, tends to get arranged in reference to it. That makes the size, frame, and fabric choices here more consequential than on almost any other item in the house. Every piece in this collection is made to order at our workshop in Lahore, cut and upholstered only after you confirm the design, not pulled from a warehouse shelf.</p>
<h2>What Holds Up and What Does Not</h2>
<p>Fabric and silhouette get most of the attention when people shop for a 3 seater sofa, but the part that decides whether it still feels solid in five years sits underneath. Solid wood frames keep their joints tight under years of daily sitting and standing, where weaker materials start to creak and loosen. Cushioning quality matters just as much: foam that compresses flat within months looks identical to good foam on day one, which is exactly why so many buyers get this wrong. Across this collection, frames carry a 2.5-year warranty and the high-density foam cushioning carries 5 years, reflecting how this piece gets more daily contact than almost any other seat in the house.</p>
<h2>Designs and Dimensions in This Collection</h2>
<p>The range spans the styles Pakistani buyers search for most: curved and boucle-finished pieces for contemporary living rooms, channel tufted and chesterfield-leaning designs for more formal drawing rooms, and L shape configurations for corner placement where an open floor plan calls for it. Sizing varies more than most buyers expect. A standard 3 seater typically runs close to 6 to 7 feet in width, but depth, arm style, and back height shift the actual footprint enough that measuring your space before ordering is worth the extra five minutes. Each product page lists exact dimensions for this reason.</p>
<p>Comparing a 3 seater sofa price in Pakistan across different sellers usually comes down to these dimensions more than the photo. A wider, deeper sofa built on a proper frame will outlast a narrower one built lighter, even when the listed price looks similar on paper.</p>
<h2>Picking the Right Fit for Your Room</h2>
<p>Smaller living rooms tend to suit the curved and lower-arm designs in this collection better than boxy chesterfield silhouettes, since the visual weight of a sofa changes how a room reads even when the floor footprint is similar. Larger drawing rooms can carry more presence, and the channel tufted and wood frame pieces hold their own better against high ceilings and bigger walls. Somewhere in between, most households end up choosing based on how the room is used day to day rather than how it looks empty in a photo.</p>
<p>Fabric choice affects daily life more than buyers usually plan for. Boucle and chenille resist visible wear well in dusty environments and stay comfortable through Lahore summers, while velvet adds a more formal look but shows pile marks if not brushed occasionally. We can talk you through which fabric suits your household over WhatsApp before you commit to a colour.</p>
<h2>Building Toward a Larger Set</h2>
<p>A 3 seater rarely stays the only seating in the room for long. It is usually paired with a 2 seater, a pair of accent chairs, or built up into a larger 5 seater or 7 seater arrangement as the household grows or the room gets reorganised. Buying with that future arrangement in mind is worth a moment''s thought, since matching frame height, arm style, and fabric across pieces bought months or years apart is much easier when the first one was chosen with that in mind. Several designs in this collection share consistent leg styles and fabric ranges with our 2 seater sofas specifically so the two can be matched without a visible mismatch.</p>
<h2>How Ordering Works</h2>
<p>Choosing a design and fabric colour happens directly with us over WhatsApp. Production begins once 60 percent of the price is paid in advance, with the remaining 40 percent due before delivery. Crafting and delivering a 3 seater sofa typically takes 20 to 25 working days from our Lahore workshop, and we ship across Pakistan, not only within the city.</p>
<p>Unsure which design or size fits your space? Send us your room dimensions before ordering. We would rather help you choose the right 3 seater sofa once than have you order the wrong size and live with it for years.</p>'
WHERE slug = '/seater-sofas/3-seater-sofas/' OR name ILIKE '3 Seater%';

UPDATE categories
SET content_html = '<h2>4 Seater Sofa Collection</h2>
<p>Wide enough to seat a family without committing to an L shape or modular layout, the 4 seater sofa sits in the space between a standard 3 seater and a full sectional. It is a less common size in Pakistani furniture shopping than 3 seater or 5 seater sofa sets, which is exactly why getting it right matters: there are fewer reference points to compare against, so design and build quality carry more weight in the decision. Every 4 seater sofa in this collection is made to order at our workshop in Lahore.</p>
<h2>Why One Long Sofa Sometimes Beats a Set</h2>
<p>A 5 seater or 6 seater sofa set usually arrives as multiple pieces, a 3 seater plus a loveseat or armchairs, arranged around a room. A 4 seater is one continuous piece instead, which works better where you want generous seating without breaking it into separate furniture items. Households who entertain in smaller groups but still want enough width for four people without crowding tend to land here, as do families who prefer one long sofa against a wall over a scattered arrangement of pieces.</p>
<p>Pricing this size is genuinely harder to benchmark than a 3 seater or 5 seater, simply because fewer sellers stock it, so buyers have less to compare against. What we can say with confidence is what is underneath the fabric: a solid wood frame so the extra width does not translate into extra strain on weak joints, paired with high-density foam cushioning that holds its shape across the full seat length instead of sagging in the middle, the most common failure point on wider sofas built with cheaper foam. The frame carries a 2.5-year warranty and the foam carries 5.</p>
<h2>Designs Available in This Collection</h2>
<p>Curved and boucle 4 seater sofas suit contemporary living rooms, while channel tufted and velvet designs lean more formal. L shape 4 seater layouts are also available for corner placement. Several designs in this range work well as the basis for a larger 6 seater or 8 seater arrangement too, paired with a matching 2 seater or armchairs from elsewhere in our collection, if your room calls for more total seating than one piece provides.</p>
<p>Dimensions vary noticeably across designs at this size. A 4 seater with low arms and a curved silhouette will read differently in a room than one with a tall tufted back and square arms, even at similar widths, since a piece this size is harder to reposition once it is in the house. Each product page lists full dimensions so you can check the fit against your room before ordering.</p>
<h2>Fabric Choices That Hold Up</h2>
<p>Boucle and chenille are the most requested fabrics in this collection, holding up well against daily use and Lahore''s dustier months without showing wear quickly. Velvet is available for buyers who want a more formal look, particularly on channel tufted designs, though it benefits from occasional brushing to keep the pile looking fresh. Choosing between fabrics for a piece this size is easier with a photo of your room in hand, which we can review with you over WhatsApp.</p>
<h2>Who This Size Actually Suits</h2>
<p>Generous seating without sectional complexity is the main draw here, along with living rooms that have one long uninterrupted wall rather than a corner to build an L shape around. Buyers who find a standard 3 seater slightly short for their family but do not want the visual weight of a full 6 or 7 seater set dominating the room also tend to choose this size. Because it sits between two more commonly searched categories, it often ends up being the better fit for a specific room even when buyers start out looking at 3 seater or 5 seater options instead.</p>
<h2>How to Order</h2>
<p>Confirming your design and fabric colour happens directly with us over WhatsApp. Production begins once 60 percent of the price is paid in advance, with the remaining 40 percent due before dispatch. Crafting and delivering a 4 seater sofa typically takes 20 to 25 working days from our Lahore workshop, with delivery available across Pakistan, not limited to Lahore alone.</p>
<p>This size occupies more wall and floor space than a standard 3 seater, so measuring your room before ordering is worth doing properly. Send us your dimensions if you want a second opinion before committing to a design.</p>'
WHERE slug = '/seater-sofas/4-seater-sofas/' OR name ILIKE '4 Seater%';

UPDATE categories
SET content_html = '<h2>5 Seater Sofa Collection</h2>
<p>Few furniture categories get searched in Pakistan as often as the 5 seater sofa set, and the reason comes down to how Pakistani drawing rooms actually get used. It is the default scale for a household built around hosting, whether that means weekly family visits, Eid gatherings, or a wedding season where the sitting room needs to hold more people than usual. Every 5 seater sofa in this collection is made to order at our workshop in Lahore, designed to anchor a room rather than just fill it.</p>
<h2>What Actually Determines Long-Term Value</h2>
<p>Fabric and finish are usually the first thing buyers compare when shopping a 5 seater sofa price in Pakistan, but the part that decides whether the set still looks and feels right in five years sits underneath the upholstery. A wider frame under more regular weight is where joints loosen first if the construction is weak, which matters more at this size than on smaller sofas. The cushioning across this collection uses high-density foam that holds its shape across long seat runs instead of dipping in the centre after a year of use. Every frame here carries a 2.5-year warranty, with the foam backed by 5 years.</p>
<p>Both single-piece 5 seater sofas and sectional layouts appear in this collection, including curved, L shape, and U shape designs. Open living rooms where guests face inward toward each other suit a curved or crescent-shaped 5 seater particularly well, while an L shape works better against two walls in a more traditional layout. Several of the channel tufted and boucle sets here are designed as a complete suite with matching armchairs rather than a single sofa alone, for households that lean toward formal seating arrangements.</p>
<h2>Sizing and Layout Decisions</h2>
<p>Two layouts dominate 5 seater sofa design in Pakistan: a continuous long sofa, or a 3+1+1 configuration combining a 3 seater with two single armchairs. Both appear in this collection, and the right choice depends on how your room is shaped. Long walls suit a continuous 5 seater best, while a 3+1+1 set gives more flexibility to angle pieces around a coffee table or rearrange them for different gatherings.</p>
<p>This is also the size where getting the dimensions wrong is most costly. A 5 seater that is even slightly oversized for a room can make the space feel cramped rather than generous, so every product page lists full dimensions, including total width for sectional and curved pieces, to check the footprint against your room before ordering.</p>
<h2>Fabric and Finish Across the Range</h2>
<p>Boucle is the most requested finish here, holding its texture well and suiting both contemporary and warmer traditional interiors. Velvet shows up across several channel tufted and Chesterfield-leaning designs for buyers wanting a more formal drawing room centrepiece, while a smaller number of pieces use corduroy or linen-blend fabric for a more relaxed, everyday character. Rooms that see daily use rather than occasional formal seating tend to do better with boucle or a performance fabric than velvet, since it holds up better against regular contact.</p>
<h2>What to Check Before You Commit</h2>
<p>A 5 seater set is a longer-term piece of furniture than most others in the house, which makes a few extra questions worth asking before placing an order. Check whether the design you like comes as a continuous sofa or a multi-piece suite, since the two are priced and delivered differently. Confirm the fabric sample against your room''s actual lighting rather than a product photo, since boucle and velvet both shift in tone between daylight and evening light. And if guests will use this sofa more than your own household will, durability and ease of cleaning usually matter more than the most formal-looking option in the range.</p>
<h2>Ordering a 5 Seater Sofa from ComfyClub</h2>
<p>Design and fabric colour get confirmed with us directly over WhatsApp, where we can also help you decide between a continuous sofa and a sectional or 3+1+1 layout based on your room. Production begins once 60 percent of the price is paid in advance, with the remaining 40 percent due before delivery. Crafting and delivering a 5 seater sofa typically takes 25 to 30 working days from our Lahore workshop, slightly longer than smaller pieces given the scale of the build. Delivery reaches across Pakistan including Karachi, Islamabad, and Rawalpindi, not only within Lahore.</p>
<p>Not sure whether a continuous 5 seater or a sectional layout fits your room better? Send us your dimensions before ordering and we will recommend the configuration that makes the most sense for the space.</p>'
WHERE slug = '/seater-sofas/5-seater-sofas/' OR name ILIKE '5 Seater%';

SELECT name, slug, length(content_html) AS content_chars
FROM categories
WHERE slug IN ('/seater-sofas/3-seater-sofas/', '/seater-sofas/4-seater-sofas/', '/seater-sofas/5-seater-sofas/')
ORDER BY slug;
